{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Exercise Replace: Session vs Remaining Week",
  "description": "How picking a replacement exercise flows from Setcard to the scope dialog, and where a remaining-week replace has to touch the backend.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "directory": "frontend",
      "title": "Frontend Layout",
      "description": "Pages hold route-level screens, components hold the cards and dialogs, helper holds data shaping. The replace feature lives in pages/WorkoutUi.tsx (state + dialog) and components/setComponent.tsx (picker)."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 242,
      "title": "All Weeks Loaded Up Front",
      "description": "fetchAllweekdata pulls the whole mesocycle tree once per mesocycleId: every session, every sessionexercise, every set. This is why a 'remaining week' replace can be computed on the client, but also why it must be persisted server-side to survive a reload."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 270,
      "title": "Current Session and Storage Key",
      "description": "The URL weeknumber/daynumber pick one session out of data.sessions. storageKey scopes the local draft per day, so edits on one day never leak into another day's draft on their own."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/helper/copySessiondata.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Isolated Working Copy",
      "description": "copySessionData deep-copies sessionexercise and set and resets feedback. sessionData is the editable draft; data stays the untouched server snapshot. Any remaining-week logic that updates other days must not mutate data by accident."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 279,
      "title": "Saved Draft Wins",
      "description": "On mount, a localStorage draft for this day overrides the server copy, otherwise the fetched session is copied in. Gotcha: if a replace is only written to React state, reloading this day restores the old exercise from the saved draft."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/components/setComponent.tsx",
      "line": 135,
      "title": "Picker Hands Off the Exercise",
      "description": "Selecting an exercise calls replaceExercise(exerciseData.exerciseId, exercise). Note the first argument is the global exercise ID, not the sessionexercise row ID; the parent uses it to find every row to rewrite. The picker only offers exercises from the same muscle group."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 184,
      "title": "Replace Request Opens the Scope Dialog",
      "description": "replaceExercise does no mutation. It stores { oldId, newExercise } in replacePrompt, which renders the dialog. This is the single entry point for both scopes, so any new scope branch starts here."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 386,
      "title": "The Remaining Week Button",
      "description": "This button is the unfinished branch: it only toasts 'not available yet' and closes the dialog. Its counterpart below calls replaceForThisSession. This is where replaceTheRemainingWeek belongs."
    },
    {
      "file": "frontend/pages/WorkoutUi.tsx",
      "line": 189,
      "title": "Session-Only Replace (Reference Implementation)",
      "description": "replaceForThisSession swaps exerciseId and exercise, keeps the set count, blanks weight/reps/rir and resets status. It only touches the in-memory draft; nothing is sent to the server. Use this as the shape for the remaining-week rewrite, but target other sessions as well."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/src/helper/fetchall.ts",
      "line": 3,
      "title": "What the Server Returns",
      "description": "The mesocycle query includes sessions with their sessionexercise rows and sets. Each session owns its own sessionexercise rows, so the same exercise for the same muscle appears as a different row ID in every week/day. Replacing 'the exercise for the remaining week' means one update per matching row across the remaining sessions."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/prisma/schema.prisma",
      "line": 51,
      "title": "The Row That Actually Changes",
      "description": "sessionexercise carries exerciseId plus workoutid (the session). Sets hang off sessionexercise, not the exercise library. So a swap is an exerciseId update on each remaining sessionexercise row; the set rows can stay as scheduled progressions unless you also want to blank them."
    },
    {
      "file": "backend/src/route/Exercise.ts",
      "line": 14,
      "title": "Existing Stub for Persistence",
      "description": "A POST /api/training/replace route was started but currently just returns the exercise list. A real remaining-week replace needs this route to write sessionexercise.exerciseId for the targeted future sessions, or it will be lost on the next fetch."
    },
    {
      "title": "Next Move",
      "description": "Decide the scope contract (rest of this week only, or every remaining week), then implement one server write plus the client call and state refresh. The session-only path already shows the local shape; the backend stub is the persistence hook."
    }
  ]
}
